<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cōs</span></b> , cōtis,
			f.
		Sanscr. ça, to whet, sharpen; cf. cautes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>any hard stone,
				flintstone</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 17, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 36,
				4</span></i> and 5; <i><span class="en">Curt. 4, 6, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 3, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 11, 23</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 8,
				43</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>a whetstone, hone,
			grindstone</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 36, 22, 47, § 164</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				C. 2, 8, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 12,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipsam iracundiam fortitudinis quasi cotem esse
					dicebant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 44, 135</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 4, 19, 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. A. P.
			304</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
